    {
      "id": 65572,
      "name": "brytehfryguy",
      "username": "brytehfryguy",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/f0a364/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-06-10T22:01:57.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Why  wouldn't  you reshuffle your deck when you need to draw a card and there are none left? Are there games where you can't?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>In the old Decipher LotR game, when you ran out, you just didn't draw cards any more. Same in Netrunner as a Runner, the Corp loses from decking. MTG, Yu-gi-oh, Pokemon all have you lose when you fail to draw a card. It's actually probably more common in popular games than not.</p>\n<div>&nbsp;</div><div>I strangely know people who have expressed annoyance that decking didn't mean you lost in Sentinels, presumably because it is just that common in other deck based games.</div>",
      "post_number": 11,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:43:02.459Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
