    {
      "id": 65574,
      "name": "Ameena",
      "username": "Ameena",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-06-11T10:13:22.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I've never played any of those games, which might be why I've not come across that particular mechanic before (actually, I have once - in an online card game I play regularly called Elements...I only play against AI though). Apart from playing a whole load of games with...erm...\"traditional\" (for want of a better word) cards whilst growing up, I didn't really start playing any Fantasy-type ones until a year ago, when I was introduced to Ascension, Chrononauts, Braggart, and of course Sentinels of the Multiverse at a gaming club. Ascension and Sentinels are the only ones where you have your own deck, and in both you reshuffle when it runs out.</p>",
      "post_number": 13,
      "post_type": 1,
